# PCBZ render server patch 0013: the model's long step can be stopped from the control channel.
# Why: the plugin's per-call budget and the person's Stop this turn both need to end one model step
# without killing the editor. The render server already answers the model's `engine.execute` calls
# on the editor's own session; `pcb.check_design` (and the other commands the editor defers) runs
# on a worker thread, so its answer arrives while the pane keeps drawing. This patch adds
# `ui.operations {cancel: "agent"}`: the control channel's socket worker handles it itself (off the
# editor's UI thread, never queued behind a frame), marks the in-flight deferred job for
# cancellation and answers {"cancelled":"agent"}; the editor's next frame stops the job's queue and
# answers the waiting engine.execute with a `stopped: ... nothing was applied` failure. A job that
# lands before the editor sees the request answers with its real result (the caller reports it as
# landed); a cancel with nothing cancellable running is refused with `no operation `agent` is under
# way`. Nothing else changes: revisions, undo history and the project file are untouched, and the
# editor process is never restarted. Read-only sessions refuse a cancel cleanly, like any other
# request with nothing to stop.
# Test-only: PCBZ_RENDER_TEST_CHECK_MS holds a deferred check on its worker for that many
# milliseconds in cancellable slices, so the render server's proof can stop a real job
# deterministically; the product never sets it (documented in PROTOCOL.md).
# Files touched: crates/app/src/live_control.rs (shared cancel state, socket-worker method, two
# answer paths) and crates/app/src/board_drc/jobs.rs (the test-only hold). CRLF and native/worker
# protocol are unchanged.

